From: Security Fix <security@example.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Disable JavaScript post aggregators to prevent RCE vulnerability

Disable JavaScript post-aggregation functions to prevent remote code execution.
JavaScript post-aggregators can be exploited to execute arbitrary system commands
through sampler requests and queries.

---
 .../aggregation/post/JavaScriptPostAggregator.java | 20 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/processing/src/main/java/org/apache/druid/query/aggregation/post/JavaScriptPostAggregator.java b/processing/src/main/java/org/apache/druid/query/aggregation/post/JavaScriptPostAggregator.java
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/processing/src/main/java/org/apache/druid/query/aggregation/post/JavaScriptPostAggregator.java
+++ b/processing/src/main/java/org/apache/druid/query/aggregation/post/JavaScriptPostAggregator.java
@@ -48,6 +48,12 @@ public class JavaScriptPostAggregator implements PostAggregator
       this.fieldNames = fieldNames;
       this.function = function;
       this.config = config;
+
+      // SECURITY FIX: Disable JavaScript post aggregators to prevent RCE
+      if (!config.isEnabled()) {
+        throw new IllegalArgumentException(
+            "JavaScript post-aggregators are disabled for security reasons. Please use other post-aggregator types.");
+      }

       final Context cx = Context.enter();
       try {
